WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.069 --> 00:00:01.231
Welcome back to Spectrum

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:04.260
This is a super highly requested episode, so we hope you guys enjoy.

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:08.220
Please stick around after the episode for a special offer from our sponsor Dashlane.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:09.820
But first, here is the episode.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.300
I don't believe in the Bible God, because he is an A-Hole.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:15.540
But I believe that in the universe, somewhere, even though there is ...

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:18.440
... a lot of evidence that there is nothing out there, there could be another dimension.

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:19.840
We don't know.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:37.260
I am open to some supernatural and spiritual ideas.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:39.020
3

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:40.000
2

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:40.900
1

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:41.500
Go

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:52.700
We've probably all had the experience of some older person saying: ''Oh well when you're on your deathbed,

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:59.320
I'm sure you'll, you'll believe, you'll want Jesus or something, and...'' Nooooo. Like I'm just-

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:02.060
I'm happy, I'm content, I'm excited about my beliefs.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:07.720
I'm open to ideas that can fit within a reasonable framework,

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:13.660
but no spiritual or supernatural idea has ever fit that standard.

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:20.000
Like I'm open to... That's why I'm like I'm that weird category of agnostic-atheism, and a lot of people were like: ''What's that?

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.080
How can you be an agnostic atheist that's weird, you're contradicting yourself.'' But I'm open to it.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.180
I don't believe in the Bible God because he's, he's an A-hole.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:32.400
But I believe that in the universe somewhere, even though there's a lot of evidence that there's nothing out there,

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.740
there could be another dimension, there could be like black holes like interstellar could go somewhere. We don't know.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:42.900
For me, you know, I'm open to wicanism and paganism, you know.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:46.500
[Giggles] It's a fun little thing to do, to see what happens.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:49.160
I think you can be atheist and spiritual too.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:54.400
You can have different beliefs. I've had some crazy Ouija board experiences. I believe in ...

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:57.220
... something else. I don't believe in someone else.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:01.170
I believe as above so below I think everything is very connected

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:04.600
and I believe that I should behave in a way that I would want

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:13.140
acted towards back to me and I think that's a very spiritual idea, you know, that the energy is recycled and that our actions invite actions.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.580
Praying is a waste of time.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.680
Three. Two. One. Go.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:25.320
Do I think it's a waste of time.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:40.440
Prayer is, people argue very often to me, that prayer brings a lot of comfort and has meaning to them.

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:45.360
You know why it has to be that over all of the other options you can do?

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:50.200
I don't know and when considering that, in a lot of cases,

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:58.640
you're choosing to step back. You're choosing to remove your responsibility from any situation.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:00.640
Yeah, I have issues with that.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:05.700
Nothing aggravates me more, too, like especially like our current political climate, when a group of people is gunned down

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:12.820
and our public and politician tweets out like: ''Sending thoughts and prayers.'' But at the same time, I'm on the somewhat disagree side because I

00:03:13.449 --> 00:03:16.769
personally think praying will not accomplish anything.

00:03:17.049 --> 00:03:23.399
But I think that what someone has to do to put positive energy out into their life and start their day

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:28.409
and I know that my parents pray for me every night and it makes me happy but I think like they're

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:31.740
sending out positive thoughts.

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:35.340
I grew up religious.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:39.100
Three. Two. One. Go.

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:50.760
I was born into Catholicism, I was born into a Catholic family. I think the majority of religion is

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:57.340
indoctrination of children, it's just by happenstance of where you're born, what religion you're born into and who

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.860
your parents happen to be.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:02.920
I grew up in a very quintessential Jew-ish household,

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:06.540
but I did go on birthright when I was 18

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:11.960
and I think that was a big factor in my atheism because while I was on that trip

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:14.500
I asked a lot of questions, which I think you're supposed to do to get out of it,

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:19.920
and all I could think about was how I was a couple miles over I might be praying to Allah instead of Hashem.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:23.820
I couldn't find a difference in my God vs another god or

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:28.720
justification for why my God was more likely of existing than another god.

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:30.280
For me growing up Mormon

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:36.420
it was just really oppressive. It was basically your life and your whole identity and

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:42.800
everyone that you even had to just hang out with or just be around was Mormon

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:45.740
You don't have a choice, basically

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:47.060
It's been a struggle for me.

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:49.020
I left when I was 18 years old.

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:52.040
I wouldn't have it any other way honestly,

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:57.980
because I just I do not like to believe in a lie.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.900
Mormonism is a lie and it's a fraud.

00:05:02.289 --> 00:05:03.340
Yeah.

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:06.599
I think we're very close, on like the same spectrum,

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:13.360
but I grew up born and raised Jehovah's Witness believing- Believing that Jehovah was God. Believing that, you know,

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:18.820
Armageddon was gonna come and if you weren't a Jehovah's Witness and we didn't convert everyone else Jehovah's Witnesses they were gonna die.

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:22.320
You believe this way: No holidays. No birthdays. No, no Christmas.

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:25.200
No blood transfusions. Like thousands of people have died

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:26.080
- Dangerous.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:26.580
of some of these beliefs

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:33.480
for no reason. I know many people have died and they shouldn't have. This is for no reason.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:35.020
But,

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:40.880
[Choked up] I'm glad that I'm out because that's really scary.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:46.640
Was super religious and once I was out, it was like a relief on my shoulders because part of me when I got this fellowship

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:51.320
was like: ''Oh shit!'' You know, my life is all new. You lose your family. You lose your support system. Everyone kicks you out.

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:53.090
You're dead.

00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:59.460
It was nice to believe that we were scammed and we were lied to and we deserve better.

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:00.240
Yeah.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.940
The world would be better off without religion.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:06.660
Three. Two. One. Go.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:12.860
Can I not?

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:15.220
[Laughter]

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:23.140
I mean all anyone has to do is just research. Just look, just read,

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:31.860
just go out there and see the harms that religion, not inherently does, but that it can and therefore does.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:36.040
Any major issue you can take in the US and

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:38.860
somehow religion will find a way to be behind that.

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:44.620
The reason why I'm standing here, despite being hurt by religion in the past, is that I feel like

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:52.080
religion brings a lot of good to like the world in general. The pros outweigh the cons in my view.

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:56.140
If there are people out there who feel like they need an instruction manual to be a good person,

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:58.140
I think they should have it.

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:02.500
The more I've thought about it, I've kind of looked at maybe large institutions,

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:12.640
power structures, dogmatic beliefs are maybe more the real problem than the really broad, big, unwieldy definition of religion.

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:15.960
The community I run is called ''Atheist United'', most people in my community

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:20.740
would love to destroy religion in the world and think the world will suddenly be better

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:25.960
but I see a bunch of atheists then, that are struggling with the same exact problems. That still have the same

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:31.900
prejudices, that deal with the same stereotypes and we just changed the label.

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:35.020
I do agree that there is community that's brought by religion,

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:38.380
but wherever there's community, there someone outside of that community.

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:40.360
There are people not accepted into that community.

00:07:40.780 --> 00:07:43.580
There's ostracism, but I think in a world where

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:48.469
there is either no religion or multitude of religions

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:54.860
there's always going to be like division in that multitude and I just don't know if the ostracism and the pain is worth

00:07:54.960 --> 00:08:00.200
the hope that the community will override that.

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:06.220
Just to push back a little bit. Given that we are tribal animals, right? We do get together

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:09.040
you know, if it's not going to be religion,

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:13.760
which I'm fine with, then it's maybe your soccer team or your chess club or your sorority.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:20.580
And my biggest concern and why I work in this community is: I don't know if you want to raise your children

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:26.240
necessarily there or if you feel like they share your values enough to help you if you're in the hospital or,

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:30.060
you know, they're the people you can turn to if you're on your deathbed.

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:32.680
Just push back a little bit too. I think that

00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:37.669
there is an issue if you think that the only group of solace that you can find for deep existential or

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:44.060
physical problems is your religious group. If they are the only people that you can turn to for help,

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:48.520
then that's a problem, because then you're feel trapped inside of them. That you can't escape that kind of group

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:49.960
and you touched on that a lot.

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:50.480
-Absolutely.

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:56.400
Having different groups with different opinions instead of one group that has one fundamental idea and said some morality.

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:58.680
You need a group that can check that morality.

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:03.320
I wish I believed in a higher power.

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:05.960
Three. Two. One. Go.

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:26.360
I don't think it would make my life easier. I would have all the same questions I have and have worse answers.

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:32.720
I think it'd be very comforting to believe in a higher power. To believe that no matter what happens, you'll be ok.

00:09:33.069 --> 00:09:38.909
I think I'd be a much happier person. But I'm also very proud of what I have accomplished on my own.

00:09:38.909 --> 00:09:42.560
I know everything that I have achieved is through my own effort.

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:46.080
Last year someone that I used to be very close with

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:53.300
died of an opioid addiction and it was like rattled my world because I'd never really been faced with the idea that like

00:09:53.740 --> 00:09:58.800
like you always know like you're gonna die one day and people die and it happens, but it just it was

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:05.980
like this like visceral reaction that we are so immortal and we are so powerless and

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:08.660
And it really messed me up

00:10:08.669 --> 00:10:13.140
and sometimes I still like wake up at night and I'm like I have to drink a lot of water and relax

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:18.720
I'm so terrified of the idea of not existing anymore. It's not the idea of dying, it's just the idea of nothing.

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:23.600
I would be upset if my children believed in God.

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:27.360
Three. Two. One. Go.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:32.040
Hmm, shit.

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:41.900
I can't be a hypocrite and say I would do the exact same thing.

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:50.500
I know what religion and the religious have done to me and others hearing all of you and say you're disowned.

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:52.340
You're no longer welcomed into my home.

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:56.380
You are no longer a part of my life.

00:10:56.980 --> 00:11:02.180
I can't do that. And so therefore I'm going to change my answer to this. [Laughs]

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:05.580
Your own relationship with God is very personal.

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:14.160
So, who am I to say who you should believe in or what you shouldn't believe in as long as you're not hurting anybody or yourself.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:18.920
Whatever is in your heart just do it. As long as you're not hurting anybody.

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:22.900
Would I be upset if my child believed in a God?

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:27.300
A little bit. [Laughter] I'm not gonna lie. I'd be like damn I didn't do a good job.

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:34.160
I agree with a lot of your guys's points, like as long as they're not hurting people, as long as you're like pursuing your happiness,

00:11:34.649 --> 00:11:37.980
Be yourself. Be happy, whatever that looks like.

00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:41.808
I also think my problem with a religious person has never been their religion.

00:11:41.809 --> 00:11:45.559
It has been like things that they have used that religion to justify.

00:11:46.139 --> 00:11:47.266
-The interpretation of it.

00:11:47.266 --> 00:11:51.109
Yeah or actions or behaviors in name of their God, you know

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:53.779
so if my child chooses to believe in God and they

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:59.500
don't use that to justify harm or malice then that's fine.

00:11:59.500 --> 00:12:04.860
Yeah, and one person I really look up to, who is kind of Christ-like is Mr. Rogers.

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:09.860
He's always been gentle and nice, you know, and he believes in God.

00:12:09.860 --> 00:12:12.800
Who am I to say "Hey, Mr. Roger, you need to stop.''?

00:12:12.860 --> 00:12:16.600
[Applause]

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:18.700
Yeah, you guy want to do lunch?

00:12:18.700 --> 00:12:19.500
Yeah.

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:21.460
I really enjoyed that discussion.

00:12:21.460 --> 00:12:25.760
Yeah, absolutely. It was really interesting to hear that some of these atheists are still open to spiritual ideas.

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:26.660
Definitely.

